keywords:
  - ocean carbon sink
  - rain
  - sea surface salinity
  - air-sea CO2 flux
  - moorings
  - MAPCO2
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  Derived data and the scripts that compute them from public raw data: 646 rain events at 13 moorings of the NOAA PMEL carbon
  mooring network (MAPCO2), 2004-2025, with observed near-surface freshening and pCO2 changes; predictions of the RIM-3 rain
  dilution scheme and the S20 surface relation of Witte et al. (2026) at the observed depths and their ratios to the
  observations; mechanism diagnostics; satellite (SMAP) and field-campaign (SPURS-1/2, PISTON) surface tests; and a
  reimplementation of the global calculation of the rain effect on the air-sea CO2 flux for the year 2000 with band, basin,
  month and wind-speed tables. The pipeline runs all stages from the raw downloads with one entry point and compares a re-run
  with the released data.
